  "Solution": {
    "S": "We have:\n\n$$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{e^{\\tan x} - e^x}{\\tan x - x} = \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{e^x (e^{\\tan x - x} - 1)}{\\tan x - x}$$\n\nAs $x \\to 0$, $e^x \\to 1$. Also, $\\tan x - x \\to 0$. Using $\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{e^h - 1}{h} = 1$, we get:\n\n$$= \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{e^{\\tan x - x} - 1}{\\tan x - x} = 1$$\n\nThus the correct option is A: 1."
  },
